(d) Judges must not engage in conduct that is prejudicial to the effective and expeditious administration of justice or the work of the Tribunal;
(e) When engaged in the administration of justice, judges must attend chambers during their normal working hours, as determined by the members of the Tribunal, and attend hearings and deliberations of the Tribunal during stipulated hours, unless they have a good reason not to do so.
Judges must inform the presiding judge of the Tribunal in advance if they need to be absent.
If they are to be absent for longer than three days, they must obtain the approval of the presiding judge of their Tribunal;
